.TH A2WCRECALC\-DMS 1 "2026-07-06" "a2tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
a2wcrecalc\-dms \- \fBa2wcrecalc\fR plus \fBdocker\-mailserver\fR mapping files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B a2wcrecalc\-dms
.RB [ \-d " " \fIDMS_DIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBa2wcrecalc\-dms\fR behaves exactly like \fBa2wcrecalc\fR(1) and then
additionally generates the per\-domain mapping files used by
\fBdocker\-mailserver\fR (\fBhttps://github.com/docker\-mailserver/docker\-mailserver\fR)
to discover which virtual host each incoming connection should be
routed to.
.PP
All arguments are named flags. The stack directory \fBDMS_DIR\fR, the
directory the mapping files are written to \fBDMS_CONFIG_DIR\fR, and the
stack owner \fBDMS_OWNER\fR are read from \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf\fR
(or any \fI*.conf\fR under \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf.d/\fR). The shipped
defaults are the podmgr layout: \fB/srv/podmgr/compose/dms\fR, its
\fBdata/config\fR, and \fBdms\fR. \fB\-d\fR / \fB\-\-dir\fR overrides
\fBDMS_DIR\fR for one run, and the mapping files then go to
\fIDMS_DIR\fB/data/config\fR.
.PP
The certificates those files point at live under the root\-only
\fB/etc/letsencrypt\fR. When \fBDMS_OWNER\fR is set to a non\-root user
(root inside a rootless container), \fBa2wcrecalc\-dms\fR grants that user
read access to each mapped certificate with \fBsetfacl\fR(1). The certbot
deploy hook runs \fBa2wcrecalc\-dms\fR after every renewal, because renewed
private keys are written with mode 0600.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIDMS_DIR\fR
Use this \fBdocker\-mailserver\fR stack directory instead of the
configured \fBDMS_DIR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the embedded usage text and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DMS_DIR
\fBdocker\-mailserver\fR stack directory (overridden by \fB\-d\fR).
.TP
.B DMS_CONFIG_DIR
Directory the container mounts as \fB/tmp/docker\-mailserver\fR.
.TP
.B DMS_OWNER
Host user owning the stack; empty for a rootful stack. For a podmgr stack:
\fBstat \-c %U /srv/podmgr/compose/dms/compose.yaml\fR.
.PP
All three are normally set in \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf\fR or a file
under \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf.d/\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR a2wcrecalc (1),
.BR a2sitemgr (1)
